description:
Design a bus hold block that maintains the output signal when the enable input is low. When the enable (en) signal is high, the output (out) follows the bus input directly; however, when en is low, the previous value of out is retained, effectively holding the output state. This functionality is useful in digital circuits where you want to prevent changes on the output until a specific control signal is activated.
module top_module(
  input bus,
  input en,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input bus,
  input en,
  output out
);reg out_reg;

  always @ (bus, en) begin
    if (en) begin
      out_reg <= bus;
    end else begin
      out_reg <= out_reg;
    end
  end

  assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

